          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+group"} Euclidean group
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            is the group generated from the rigid translation action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            on itself and rotations about the origin.
          %p
            The
            %em super Euclidean group
            is analogously the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"} supergroup
            of translations and rotations of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{p|q}
          %p
            Its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            should be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincare+Lie+algebra"} super Poincare Lie algebra
            (up to the signature of the metric).
          %h2#details Details
          %blockquote
            %p
              %strong incomplete
              for the moment, to be finished off tomorrow
          %p
            The following description of the super Euclidean group (once it is finished, and polished) is due to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stephan+Stolz"} Stephan Stolz
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Teichner"} Peter Teichner
          %p The data needed to define the super Euclidean group is
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                a
                = succeed "-dimensional" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+representation"} spinor representation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^*
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Spin
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(V)
            %li
              %p
                a
                = succeed "-equivariant" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Spin
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(V)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi ℂ
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mi V
                      %msub
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi ℝ
                      %mi ℂ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\Gamma : \Delta^* \otimes_{\mathbb{C}}
                      \\Delta^* \to V \otimes_{\mathbb{R}} \mathbb{C}
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(V)
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin+group"} Spin group
            (see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+algebra"} Clifford algebra
            for the moment).
          %p
            Here is the construction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Eucl
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Eucl(\mathbb{R}^{d|\delta})
            for
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi dim
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = dim_{\mathbb{R}} V
          %p
            %strong remark
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta
            is a multiple of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mn 2
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mfrac
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{[\frac{d-1}{2}]}
          %p set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi Π
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi V
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi Δ
                              %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi V
                    %mo )
                  %mo =
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Π
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X = \Pi
                  \\left(
                  \\array{ V \times \Delta^* \\ \downarrow \\ V}
                  \\right)
                  \=
                  V \times \Pi \Delta^*
          %p
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+supermanifold"} complex supermanifold
            of dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d|\delta)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Π
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C^\infty(V \times \Pi \Delta^*)
                  \=
                  C^\infty(V) \otimes
                  \\wedge^\bullet \Delta
                  \=
                  C^\infty(V, \wedge^\bullet(\Delta))
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta = 1
            this is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mi Δ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ev
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mi Δ
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi odd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots = C^\infty(C, \wedge^\bullet \Delta)^{ev}
                  \\oplus
                  C^\infty(C, \wedge^\bullet \Delta)^{odd}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊕
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \simeq
                  C^\infty(V) \oplus C^\infty(V, \wedge^\bullet \Delta)
          %p
            where the last factor is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ;
                  %mi Δ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \simeq C^\infty(V; \Delta) \simeq C^\infty(V, S^+)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^+
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinor+bundle"} spinor bundle
          %p now define the multiplication
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Π
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Π
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi μ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Π
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (V \times \Pi \Delta^*)
                  \\times
                  (V \times \Pi \Delta^*)
                  \\stackrel{\mu}{\to}
                  (V \times \Pi \Delta^*)
          %p
            by sayin what it does on sets of probes by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Π
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Π
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi μ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Π
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (V \times \Pi \Delta^*)(S)
                  \\times
                  (V \times \Pi \Delta^*)(S)
                  \\stackrel{\mu(S)}{\to}
                  (V \times \Pi \Delta^*)(S)
          %p here on the left we have the sets of sections
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ev
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi ev
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  C^\infty(S)^{ev} \otimes V
                  \\times
                  C^\infty(S)^{ev} \otimes \Delta^*
          %p so we can map these as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi θ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ((v_1, \theta_1),
                  (v_2, \theta_2)
                  )
                  \\mapsto
                  (v_1 + v_2 + \Gamma(\theta_1 \otimes \theta_2),
                  \\theta_1 + \theta_2)
          %p
            %strong Remark
          %p
            if the data
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo *
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V, \Delta^*, \Gamma)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Γ
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V', (\Delta^*)', \Gamma')
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
            we get compatible notions of structures
          %p
            But if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 0,1,2
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi δ
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta = 1
            then there is a
            %em unique
            such triple with non-degenerate pairing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Γ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
            up to isomorphism.
          %p
            %strong Definition
          %p
            The structure of a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+supermanifold"} Euclidean supermanifold
            on a
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi δ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (d|\delta)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            is a
            = succeed "-structure." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Π
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi End
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V \times \Pi \Delta^*, End(V, \Delta^*, \Gamma))
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            recall the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+algebra"} Clifford algebra
            table:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi d
                        %mtd
                          %mi Cl
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi ev
                        %mtd
                          %mi Spin
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℝ
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %mo ±
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℝ
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ⊕
                          %mi ℝ
                          %msub
                            %mi e
                            %mn 1
                          %msub
                            %mi e
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %msubsup
                            %mi e
                            %mi i
                            %mn 2
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi ℂ
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  d &amp; Cl(\mathbb{R}^d)^{ev} &amp; Spin(\mathbb{R}^d)
                  \\\
                  \\\
                  1 &amp; \mathbb{R} &amp; \{\pm 1\}
                  \\\
                  2 &amp; (\mathbb{R} 1 \oplus \mathbb{R} e_1 e_2, e_i^2 = 1) \simeq \mathbb{C} &amp; S^1
                  }
          %p
            the group structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %mi Π
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \times \Pi \Delta^*
            is that of the “translations” and “rotations”
          %p
            it will be defined on
            = succeed "s" do
